plan_library.instruction:
Plan day {{day}} of {{itemCount}} ({{date day}}) for {{residents}} residents at a {{join institution ", "}} facility — provide {{join Meals ", "}}.

Honor EVERY diet: {{join diets ", "}}. Stay within the legal and food-safety requirements in the context above. Keep it within a {{costTier}} budget.
{{#if preferences}}Favor resident preferences where you can: {{join preferences ", "}}.{{/if}}
Residents per diet: {{#each (allocate diets residents) as |d|}}{{d.diet}} {{d.demand}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}} (total {{residents}}).
{{#if (season (date day))}}
Use produce that is in season for {{season (date day)}}{{#if region}} in {{region}}{{/if}}.
{{/if}}
{{#if region}}{{#eq (weekday (date day)) "Friday"}}
Make today's dinner a {{region}} regional theme.
{{/eq}}{{/if}}
{{#if flags.pureed}}
Every dish must be safe to blend — use only ingredients that can go in a blender (no bones, shells, pits, hard seeds, gristle, or anything that won't puree smooth).
{{/if}}

The only functions you may call are: {{join tools ", "}}. Never call or emit a function/tool call for any other name (e.g. meal_plan, menu_planner) — output your meal plan as plain YAML content, not as a {"name": ..., "parameters": ...} object.

Propose the RAW PROTEINS this kitchen should rotate through for these diets: {{join diets ", "}}.

Propose 12 to 20 distinct proteins spanning meat, poultry, seafood, egg, dairy and plant sources so the cycle has real variety. For each, list every diet from {{join diets ", "}} it is an appropriate routine choice for, and give the reason that decided it — the rule, restriction or nutrient limit that applies.{{#if costTier}} Respect the {{costTier}} cost tier.{{/if}}{{#if region}} Respect {{region}} regional availability.{{/if}}{{#if proteinWeights}}

The chef has ALREADY chosen the proteins for this cycle — do NOT propose your own. Use EXACTLY these and classify every one of them. The number in parentheses is how much of the cycle that protein should fill, and any diets listed after it are the ones the chef marked it for:
{{proteinLines proteinWeights}}{{/if}}{{#if addedProteins}}

The chef has ALSO added these proteins by hand — include EVERY one of them in your output and classify it the same way, even if you would not have proposed it: {{join addedProteins ", "}}.{{/if}}
